.IX Title "Clownfish::ByteBuf 3pm"
.TH Clownfish::ByteBuf 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Clownfish::ByteBuf \- Growable buffer holding arbitrary bytes.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\&    my $buf = Clownfish::ByteBuf\->new($byte_string);
\&    my $byte_string = $buf\->to_perl;
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 1
\&    my $buf = Clownfish::ByteBuf\->new($byte_string);
.Ve
.PP
Create a ByteBuf containing the passed-in bytes.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS set_size
.IX Subsection "set_size"
.Vb 1
\&    $byte_buf\->set_size($size);
.Ve
.PP
Resize the ByteBuf to \f(CW\*(C`size\*(C'\fR.  If greater than the object’s capacity,
throws an error.
.SS get_size
.IX Subsection "get_size"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $byte_buf\->get_size();
.Ve
.PP
Return the size of the ByteBuf in bytes.
.SS get_capacity
.IX Subsection "get_capacity"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $byte_buf\->get_capacity();
.Ve
.PP
Return the number of bytes in the ByteBuf’s allocation.
.SS cat
.IX Subsection "cat"
.Vb 1
\&    $byte_buf\->cat($blob);
.Ve
.PP
Concatenate the contents of Blob \f(CW\*(C`blob\*(C'\fR onto the end of the
original ByteBuf. Allocate more memory as needed.
.SS yield_blob
.IX Subsection "yield_blob"
.Vb 1
\&    my $blob = $byte_buf\->yield_blob();
.Ve
.PP
Return the content of the ByteBuf as Blob and clear the ByteBuf.
.SS utf8_to_string
.IX Subsection "utf8_to_string"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string = $byte_buf\->utf8_to_string();
.Ve
.PP
Return a String which holds a copy of the UTF\-8 character data in
the ByteBuf after checking for validity.
.SS trusted_utf8_to_string
.IX Subsection "trusted_utf8_to_string"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string = $byte_buf\->trusted_utf8_to_string();
.Ve
.PP
Return a String which holds a copy of the UTF\-8 character data in
the ByteBuf, skipping validity checks.
.SS compare_to
.IX Subsection "compare_to"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $byte_buf\->compare_to($other);
.Ve
.PP
Indicate whether one ByteBuf is less than, equal to, or greater than
another.  The byte contents of the ByteBufs are compared
lexicographically.  Throws an exception if \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR is not a ByteBuf.
.PP
Returns: 0 if the ByteBufs are equal, a negative number if \f(CW\*(C`self\*(C'\fR is
less than \f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR, and a positive number if \f(CW\*(C`self\*(C'\fR is greater than
\&\f(CW\*(C`other\*(C'\fR.
.SS clone
.IX Subsection "clone"
.Vb 1
\&    my $result = $byte_buf\->clone();
.Ve
.PP
Return a clone of the object.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Clownfish::ByteBuf isa Clownfish::Obj.
